            }
          ],
          "cofactorCrossReference": {
            "database": "ChEBI",
            "id": "CHEBI:18420"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256",
              "source": "RuleBase",
              "id": "RU000352"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Dimer of alpha and beta chains. A typical microtubule is a hollow water-filled tube with an outer diameter of 25 nm and an inner diameter of 15 nM. Alpha-beta heterodimers associate head-to-tail to form protofilaments running lengthwise along the microtubule wall with the beta-tubulin subunit facing the microtubule plus end conferring a structural polarity. Microtubules usually have 13 protofilaments but different protofilament numbers can be found in some organisms and specialized cells"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "SUBUNIT"
    },
